  "result": "No, that's not right. A model remembers nothing between conversations. Each request starts blank, and it only \"knows\" what is in the text sent with that request.\n\nIt's tempting because a chat app feels continuous. That continuity comes from the app, which re-sends the earlier messages every time.\n\nFor your assistant, you have to build the memory. After a session, save the facts that matter (say, `{\"student\": \"A. Lee\", \"laser_cutter_trained\": true}`) to a file or database. At the start of the next session, look up that student's record and put it in the prompt. The model \"remembers\" last week only if your code did that.\n\nWhich facts from a visit do you think are worth saving?",
